# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  DOMINION COMPLETE — Build Roadmap (src/roadmap.pjs)
#  Generated with the Atomic Roadmap workflow
#  (perchance.org/atomic-roadmap). The landing page reads this
#  file live, so keep the [ ] / [x] task markers intact.
#
#  HOW TO USE (gated, one at a time):
#  1. Pick the FIRST uncompleted task (lowest number).
#  2. Implement ONLY that task. Add validation/tests for it.
#  3. Tick it [x]. Verify it works in the live preview.
#  4. Stop for review before the next task. Never jump ahead.
#
#  CONVENTIONS:
#  - A card task means: add the card to src/data/<set>.json with
#    official text, implement its effect, and validate with a rule
#    assertion (cost, types, triggers, edge cases) before [x].
#  - A "Pin the catalog" task means: transcribe every card (name,
#    cost, types, text, pile sizes) from the CURRENT official
#    rulebook for that set into src/data/<set>.json, and reconcile
#    this phase's roster with it (2nd-edition changes included).
#  - "Split the roster" tasks exist for later sets whose card
#    lists must be confirmed against the pinned catalog; when one
#    is reached, expand it into one atomic task per card first
#    (Atomic Roadmap Mode 2), then implement them in order.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

#### Phase 1: Core Engine & Foundation
1. **[x] Author the project skeleton and test harness:** Create src/engine.js (pure, DOM-free game logic), src/cards.js (catalog), src/ai.js, src/ui.js, src/net.js, src/data/*.json (card text), and src/tests.js — a deterministic rule-assertion suite runnable via a ?tests=1 page mode. Validate: harness runs and reports pass/fail.
2. **[x] Define the card schema and catalog registry:** Card model with id, name, cost (coins + potion), types, treasure value, VP value, effect text, expansion; register the base non-kingdom cards Copper, Silver, Gold, Estate, Duchy, Province, Curse. Validate: lookup and validation of every field.
3. **[x] Implement player zones and pile-movement helpers:** Draw, hand, discard, play area per player, and one shared trash, with move helpers that enforce zone invariants. Validate: zone transfers are exact and impossible moves are rejected.
4. **[x] Implement drawing with exact reshuffle rules:** Draw N; when the deck empties mid-draw, shuffle the discard into the deck and continue; when both are empty, draw nothing. Use a seeded shuffle for tests. Validate: deck/discard edge cases, including a 5-card deck against a 7-card draw.
5. **[x] Implement the turn state machine and resources:** Phases Start → Action → Buy → Cleanup → Draw; resources +Cards/+Actions/+Buys/+Coins/+Potions; the one-action-per-turn limit; phase-entry/exit hooks. Validate: resource math and phase ordering in a full turn.
6. **[x] Implement Treasure play and coin totals:** Playing Treasures from hand adds coins; hook for auto-play in the UI. Validate: coin totals from mixed Treasures (Copper/Silver/Gold) are exact.
7. **[x] Implement playing an Action from hand:** Legality check (actions available), effect resolution, move to play area, cleanup to discard. Validate: the play-action pipeline for a Village and a Smithy.
8. **[x] Implement the Buy step:** Affordability (coins + potions, debt rules reserved for later), purchase from a supply pile, gain-to-discard, pile-empty behavior, buy-count limit. Validate: purchases are correct and empty piles are un-buyable.
9. **[x] Implement the Attack framework:** 'Each other player' iteration, the reaction window (Reaction cards can be revealed before the attack resolves), and unaffected outcomes. Validate: Witch, Militia and Moat interact correctly.
10. **[x] Implement end-of-game detection and scoring:** Game ends when 3 supply piles are empty or the Province pile empties; score all VP sources including dynamic ones (Gardens, Duke, Vineyard, Fairgrounds) plus VP tokens. Validate: a fixture game scores exactly.
11. **[x] Implement supply setup by player count:** Starting decks (7 Copper, 3 Estate), pile sizes (Copper 60, Silver 40, Gold 30; Victory/Curse 8 at 2p, 12 at 3–4p), and the 10 Kingdom piles from the chosen set. Validate: counts for 2, 3, and 4 players.
12. **[x] Implement effect primitives and the trigger registry:** gain, trash, reveal, topdeck, discard-at-cost, play-another, choose-X primitives; when-gained/trashed/bought/played/start-of-turn hooks, expansion-ready. Validate: trigger ordering for a gain-with-bonus chain.
13. **[x] Implement deterministic RNG and the game log:** Seeded random source for every shuffle/selection in the engine (no direct Math.random in game logic), plus a move log for replay and validation. Validate: identical seeds produce identical games.

#### Phase 2: Base Game — Dominion (2nd Edition)
14. **[x] Implement Artisan:** Action, $6: Gain a card costing up to $5, putting it into your hand. Validate effect, cost math, and zone placement.
15. **[x] Implement Bandit:** Action-Attack, $5: Gain a Gold; each other player reveals the top 2 of their deck, trashes a revealed Treasure other than Copper, discards the rest. Validate vs the attack framework.
16. **[x] Implement Bureaucrat:** Action-Attack, $4: Gain a Silver onto your deck; each other player reveals a Victory card and puts it on top (or reveals a hand with none). Validate.
17. **[x] Implement Cellar:** Action, $2: +1 Action; discard any number of cards, then draw that many. Validate discard-then-draw counts.
18. **[x] Implement Chapel:** Action, $2: Trash up to 4 cards from your hand. Validate 0-to-4 trashing.
19. **[x] Implement Council Room:** Action, $5: +4 Cards; +1 Buy; each other player draws 1 card. Validate the shared-benefit attack iteration.
20. **[x] Implement Festival:** Action, $5: +2 Actions; +1 Buy; +2 Coins. Validate resource math.
21. **[x] Implement Gardens:** Victory, $4: Worth 1 VP per 10 cards in your deck (rounded down). Validate scoring at 9/10/19/20 cards.
22. **[x] Implement Harbinger:** Action, $3: +1 Card; +1 Action; look at the top card of your discard pile, you may topdeck it. Validate.
23. **[x] Implement Laboratory:** Action, $5: +2 Cards; +1 Action. Validate.
24. **[x] Implement Library:** Action, $5: Draw to 7 cards, setting aside any Action cards revealed, discarding the set-asides when you stop. Validate the set-aside flow.
25. **[x] Implement Market:** Action, $5: +1 Card; +1 Action; +1 Buy; +1 Coin. Validate.
26. **[x] Implement Merchant:** Action, $3: +1 Card; +1 Action; the first Silver you play this turn gives +1 Coin. Validate the Silver-flag rule.
27. **[x] Implement Militia:** Action-Attack, $4: +2 Coins; each other player discards down to 3 cards. Validate discard-to-3.
28. **[x] Implement Mine:** Action, $5: Trash a Treasure from hand; gain a Treasure costing up to 3 more into your hand. Validate cost-up-to-3 and hand placement.
29. **[x] Implement Moat:** Action-Reaction, $2: +2 Cards; when an opponent plays an Attack, reveal to be unaffected. Validate the reaction window.
30. **[x] Implement Moneylender:** Action, $4: Trash a Copper from hand for +3 Coins. Validate the conditional bonus.
31. **[x] Implement Poacher:** Action, $4: +1 Card; +1 Action; +1 Coin; each other player discards a card for each empty supply pile. Validate the empty-pile interaction.
32. **[x] Implement Remodel:** Action, $4: Trash a card from hand; gain a card costing up to 2 more. Validate.
33. **[x] Implement Sentry:** Action, $5: +1 Card; +1 Action; look at the top 2 cards, trash/discard/topdeck any of them. Validate each disposal path.
34. **[x] Implement Smithy:** Action, $4: +3 Cards. Validate.
35. **[x] Implement Throne Room:** Action, $4: Play an Action card from your hand twice. Validate double-resolution incl. chained Throne Rooms.
36. **[x] Implement Vassal:** Action, $3: +2 Coins; reveal the top of your deck; if it is an Action, play it (otherwise discard). Validate.
37. **[x] Implement Village:** Action, $3: +1 Card; +2 Actions. Validate.
38. **[x] Implement Witch:** Action-Attack, $5: +2 Cards; each other player gains a Curse. Validate Curse pile depletion.

#### Phase 3: Tabletop UI & Interaction
39. **[x] Render the card component:** DOM card showing cost, types, name, effect text and expansion badge; hand-fan layout with hover-to-enlarge; supply piles with price tags and counts. Validate visually with the vision tool.
40. **[x] Build the table layout:** Supply area, trash, player zones (draw/discard/play/hand), turn banner and phase indicators; responsive from phone to 6-player wide. Validate visually.
41. **[x] Wire click interactions:** Play Action from hand, play Treasures (auto or manual), buy from supply, end-phase buttons; disabled states when illegal. Validate a full turn by click.
42. **[x] Implement the choice/modal system:** Pick-a-card, pick-up-to-N, pick-an-opponent and options-list prompts (needed by nearly every expansion card). Validate with Remodel and Sentry.
43. **[x] Build opponent and status panels:** Deck/hand/discard counts, coin/action/buy trackers, VP and Curse counts, live game log. Validate against engine state.
44. **[x] Add expansion zone surfaces:** Duration row, Reserve/Tavern mat, Exile mat, and Debt/Villager/Coffers token trays. Validate they render from engine state.
45. **[x] Build the end-game screen:** Per-source VP breakdown, winner announcement, play-again action. Validate with a fixture game.
46. **[x] Add animations:** Card movement (draw/play/buy/trash/gain), supply depletion states, turn transitions; honors prefers-reduced-motion. Validate visually.
47. **[x] Hotseat smoke test:** A complete 2-player game from setup to scoring with no console or engine errors. Validate via browser_eval + vision.

#### Phase 4: AI Opponents
48. **[x] Implement the AI interface and action-play selection:** Evaluate legal plays by value; play actions greedily (Village chains, Smithy draws) with attack timing. Validate: AI completes turns without errors.
49. **[x] Build the buy decision model:** Per-card value scoring from deck state, with Easy/Normal/Hard weight tiers. Validate: harder tiers buy more consistently.
50. **[x] Add the Brutal tier:** Short lookahead simulation of next-turn value for buy decisions. Validate against a fixed fixture kingdom.
51. **[x] Implement choice-card policies:** Which card to gain/trash/discard/topdeck and when to use Attacks. Validate on Militia, Remodel, Sentry, Mine.
52. **[x] Handle special-state AI:** Durations, reserves, Potion/debt/coin-token optimization, and greening (when to stop buying and buy VP). Validate in a long AI game.
53. **[x] Harden AI:** Infinite-loop guards, seeded determinism for tests, configurable play speed, difficulty wired into setup. Validate with a 6-AI-headless game.

#### Phase 5: Setup, Encyclopedia & Meta
54. **[x] Build the setup screen:** Player count (2–6), names, AI difficulty, expansion toggles, random vs manual kingdom. Validate all combinations start a game.
55. **[x] Implement the kingdom picker:** Search/filter every card by name, type, cost, expansion; select exactly 10; surface required extras (Bane, Heirlooms, Potion). Validate selection rules.
56. **[x] Build the card encyclopedia:** Searchable reference of all implemented cards with full official text. Validate every registered card appears.
57. **[x] Build the rules and how-to-play modal:** Turn structure, phases, and a glossary of every engine keyword. Validate content renders.
58. **[x] Add first-turn onboarding:** A guided first turn highlighting play/buy/cleanup. Validate the tutorial completes.
59. **[x] Seeded kingdoms and shareable setup URLs:** Same seed → same kingdom deterministically; ?kingdom= URLs restore setup. Validate determinism.

#### Phase 6: Persistence & Settings
60. **[x] Autosave and resume with the kv-plugin:** Persist running single-player games and restore them on load. Validate: a saved mid-turn game restores exactly.
61. **[x] Settings persistence:** Theme, animation toggle, sound, default expansion set. Validate they survive a reload.
62. **[x] Saved kingdoms and player stats:** Favorite kingdoms; win/loss and score history per difficulty. Validate via kv entries.
63. **[x] Export/import game state:** Game-state JSON export and import for replay or sharing. Validate a round-trip.

#### Phase 7: Intrigue (2nd Edition)
64. **[x] Pin the official Intrigue (2nd Edition) catalog:** Transcribe all 26 kingdom cards into src/data/intrigue.json and reconcile this phase's roster. Validate the file matches the rulebook.
65. **[x] Implement Conspirator:** Action, $4: +$2; if you have played 3+ Actions this turn, +1 Card and +1 Action. Validate.
66. **[x] Implement Courtier:** Action, $5: Reveal a card from hand; for each type it has choose a distinct bonus (+1 Action, +1 Buy, +$3, or gain a Gold). Validate type counting.
67. **[x] Implement Courtyard:** Action, $2: +3 Cards; put a card from hand on top of your deck. Validate.
68. **[x] Implement Diplomat:** Action-Reaction, $4: +2 Cards; if you have 5 or fewer cards in hand (after drawing), +2 Actions; Reaction to an opponent Attack (reveal from a hand of 5+) draws 2 then discards 3. Validate.
