70. **[x] Implement Farmland:** Victory, $6: 2 VP; when you buy this, you may trash a card from hand and gain a card costing up to 2 more. Validate the on-buy trigger. (Note: Farmland is a Hinterlands card, implemented here per this task; its data lives in src/data/hinterlands.json.)
71. **[x] Implement Harem:** Treasure-Victory, $6: +2 Coins; worth 2 VP. Validate dual-type handling.
72. **[x] Implement Ironworks:** Action, $4: Gain a card costing up to $4; if it is an Action +1 Action, a Treasure +1 Coin, a Victory +1 Card. Validate type bonuses.
73. **[x] Implement Lurker:** Action, $2: Choose one: trash an Action from the Supply, or gain an Action from the Trash. Validate supply/trash interaction.
74. **[x] Implement Masquerade:** Action, $3: +2 Cards; each player passes a card from hand to the left; then you may trash a card from hand. Validate the pass step incl. empty hands.
75. **[x] Implement Mill:** Action-Victory, $4: +1 Card; +1 Action (roadmap text said +2 Actions — official is +1); worth 1 VP; you may discard 2 cards for +2 Coins. Validate.
76. **[x] Implement Mining Village:** Action, $4: +1 Card; +2 Actions; you may trash this for +2 Coins. Validate self-trash timing.
77. **[x] Implement Minion:** Action-Attack, $5: +1 Action; choose +2 Coins, or make every player with 5+ cards discard and draw 4. Validate both modes.
78. **[x] Implement Nobles:** Action-Victory, $6: 2 VP; choose +3 Cards or +2 Actions. Validate.
79. **[x] Implement Pawn:** Action, $2 (roadmap said $1 — official is $2): Choose two different: +1 Card, +1 Action, +1 Buy, +1 Coin. Validate pair selection.
80. **[x] Implement the pinned card for the 'Patron' slot:** the Intrigue 2E card is Patrol (Action, $5: +3 Cards; reveal the top 4; Victory cards and Curses to hand; the rest back in any order) — the roadmap's "Patron" is a Seaside card. Validated per pinned text.
81. **[x] Implement Replace:** Action-Attack, $5: Trash a card from hand; gain a card costing up to 2 more; if it is an Action or Treasure put it on your deck, if it is a Victory card each other player gains a Curse (roadmap said 'each other player does the same' — official is the Curse gain). Validate.
82. **[x] Implement Secret Passage:** Action, $4: +2 Cards; +1 Action (roadmap omitted it — official has it); put a card from hand anywhere in your deck. Validate deck placement.
83. **[x] Implement Shanty Town:** Action, $3: +2 Actions; reveal your hand; if it contains no Actions, +2 Cards. Validate.
84. **[x] Implement Steward:** Action, $3: Choose +2 Cards, or +2 Coins, or trash 2 cards from hand. Validate all three modes.
85. **[x] Implement Swindler:** Action-Attack, $3: +2 Coins; each other player trashes the top card of their deck and gains a card with the same cost that you choose (2E; roadmap said 'costing exactly 1 less' — that is the 1E text). Validate the exact-cost rule.
86. **[x] Implement Torturer:** Action-Attack, $5: +3 Cards; each other player chooses: discard 2 cards or gain a Curse. Validate both choices.
87. **[x] Implement Trading Post:** Action, $5: Trash 2 cards from hand; gain a Silver into hand. Validate.
88. **[x] Implement Upgrade:** Action, $3: Trash a card from hand; gain a card costing exactly 1 more. Validate.
89. **[x] Implement Wishing Well:** Action, $3: +1 Card; +1 Action; name a card, reveal the top of your deck, draw it if it matches. Validate.

